WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:02.218
- [Announcer] Middle Ground
is a social experiment

00:00:02.218 --> 00:00:04.554
that brings humans with
opposing beliefs together.

00:00:04.554 --> 00:00:06.374
These discussions may contain viewpoints

00:00:06.374 --> 00:00:08.308
that are the result of misinformation.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.577
Remember to seek out
experts and to be critical

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.959
of your own biases while
forming an opinion.

00:00:12.959 --> 00:00:15.504
Please see the humanity
in each participant

00:00:15.504 --> 00:00:18.504
and as always, we encourage empathy.

00:00:21.157 --> 00:00:24.018
- So when you say we're just
redefining what being a man is,

00:00:24.018 --> 00:00:26.678
you have to understand you're
redefining a fabric in society

00:00:26.678 --> 00:00:28.353
that has kept the human race

00:00:28.353 --> 00:00:30.314
and got it to where it is today.

00:00:30.314 --> 00:00:32.773
- But do you see the
state of our world today?

00:00:32.773 --> 00:00:33.710
It's not perfect.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.900
And it's been led by men
throughout all of history

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.356
and look where it's gone.

00:00:38.356 --> 00:00:40.939
(mellow music)

00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:52.540
- [Announcer] Step forward
if you agree with the prompt.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.957
"Masculinity is disappearing in America."

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.592
- I think that masculinity
is disappearing.

00:01:03.592 --> 00:01:05.116
I think that it's a concerted effort,

00:01:05.116 --> 00:01:06.616
to emasculate men,

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:11.556
I think that some people feel
threatened by masculinity

00:01:11.556 --> 00:01:14.725
and the typical way that
men carry themselves,

00:01:14.725 --> 00:01:17.022
leading families and
different things like that.

00:01:17.022 --> 00:01:18.781
So I think that there's a effort

00:01:18.781 --> 00:01:21.809
to mitigate strong men in America.

00:01:21.809 --> 00:01:23.821
- There's a few different ways
to think about masculinity.

00:01:23.821 --> 00:01:28.029
But just looking at the definition
of the term 50 years ago.

00:01:28.029 --> 00:01:29.752
You had people like John Wayne,

00:01:29.752 --> 00:01:32.725
you had Martin Luther
King, you had Sean Connery.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.789
You think of like masculine
features as in beards,

00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:38.610
hairy chest, big muscles
think stoic, being brave,

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.335
being rugged, being a provider.

00:01:41.335 --> 00:01:44.245
Today you have people like Harry Styles

00:01:44.245 --> 00:01:45.436
and Timothée Chalamet.

00:01:45.436 --> 00:01:47.348
You have people that
are completely contrary

00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:49.730
to what we were looking at back then

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.211
and those values of those
masculine characteristics

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.969
are completely devalued.

00:01:53.969 --> 00:01:56.631
- I do believe that
masculinity is going downhill,

00:01:56.631 --> 00:01:59.568
especially if you look at
like the testosterone levels.

00:01:59.568 --> 00:02:01.996
Now the testosterone levels
for guys is going down,

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:03.732
compared to generations before us.

00:02:03.732 --> 00:02:05.312
So, yeah, I agree.

00:02:05.312 --> 00:02:06.453
(whoosh air)

00:02:06.453 --> 00:02:07.303
- Hi, I'm Gilbert.

00:02:07.303 --> 00:02:08.647
I'm 24 years old and
I'm a conservative man.

00:02:08.647 --> 00:02:11.477
With my beliefs and having
a trans man as my friend.

00:02:11.477 --> 00:02:13.251
We don't really talk about politics.

00:02:13.251 --> 00:02:15.380
Someone being trans doesn't make me

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:17.302
like them any less of a person.

00:02:17.302 --> 00:02:20.196
As far as pronouns, when
referring to my friend,

00:02:20.196 --> 00:02:23.961
I don't really use the pronouns
that my friend would want.

00:02:23.961 --> 00:02:26.953
I just say my friend or I say their name,

00:02:26.953 --> 00:02:28.850
just because I feel like I'm
giving into the narrative

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.983
that men can be women and women can be men

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:34.066
if I use the pronouns that they want.

00:02:38.523 --> 00:02:41.382
- I do see that masculinity
is under attack completely.

00:02:41.382 --> 00:02:43.348
But my definition of
masculinity, like you said,

00:02:43.348 --> 00:02:45.668
has a lot to do with the traits
that are associated with it.

00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:47.648
As a gay man (chuckles) of all of us,

00:02:47.648 --> 00:02:49.436
I'm not the most masculine man.

00:02:49.436 --> 00:02:52.504
But I do think that the
good aspects of masculinity

00:02:52.504 --> 00:02:53.938
are definitely under attack.

00:02:53.938 --> 00:02:55.451
But I don't think that it's disappearing,

00:02:55.451 --> 00:02:57.875
it's just being channeled
in different ways.

00:02:57.875 --> 00:02:59.133
- It depends on how you look at it,

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:00.513
because a lot of the traits

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:03.627
can also be embodied in
women and in femininity.

00:03:03.627 --> 00:03:05.470
So when we look at masculinity,

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:08.143
I think that we have to also look at

00:03:08.143 --> 00:03:11.656
what is the actual definition
of femininity and masculinity.

00:03:11.656 --> 00:03:15.207
And if we're defining
masculinity by being stoic

00:03:15.207 --> 00:03:18.023
or muscles or body parts,

00:03:18.023 --> 00:03:20.638
then is it really masculinity?

00:03:20.638 --> 00:03:22.493
- A lot of times when you
guys spoke about masculinity,

00:03:22.493 --> 00:03:24.241
you associated with men being manly.

00:03:24.241 --> 00:03:26.992
But I think more women are
embracing their masculinity.

00:03:26.992 --> 00:03:27.825
Masculinity is still there.

00:03:27.825 --> 00:03:30.296
I mean, just other genders are using it.

00:03:30.296 --> 00:03:31.438
Being courageous, being powerful,

00:03:31.438 --> 00:03:33.671
more women are standing in their power,

00:03:33.671 --> 00:03:35.359
which is again associated masculine,

00:03:35.359 --> 00:03:37.360
but it's not specific to just men.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.732
Women are no longer submissive,
they're are dominant.

00:03:39.732 --> 00:03:40.775
Women don't need men.

00:03:40.775 --> 00:03:43.556
And I think that most
of America's realizing

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.526
that anyone can be powerful on their own.

00:03:45.526 --> 00:03:49.128
- I believe that the masculine
traits are inherently in men

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.697
and men have to take a position.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:51.530
You made a really good point

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.957
by saying women are now
becoming more masculine.

00:03:53.957 --> 00:03:55.999
They feel as if they don't need men,

00:03:55.999 --> 00:03:58.428
which I think is the problem here.

00:03:58.428 --> 00:04:02.615
I think that the way we been
designed by God, in my opinion,

00:04:02.615 --> 00:04:05.195
is that men are to lead,
men are to be strong,

00:04:05.195 --> 00:04:06.336
men are to be brave,

00:04:06.336 --> 00:04:08.170
men have to take their rightful position.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:11.823
The way our country has been
structured to this point

00:04:11.823 --> 00:04:14.668
have been because of strong
men who have taken a stand,

00:04:14.668 --> 00:04:15.870
who have fought wars.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.914
Now I feel like it's getting so lopsided

00:04:17.914 --> 00:04:20.695
that our families are degrading,

00:04:20.695 --> 00:04:22.631
people don't know where
they're at in this country.

00:04:22.631 --> 00:04:26.265
- Now in 2022, masculinity
is being redefined.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.400
And I think what happens
is people get upset

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.452
when things start to change.

00:04:30.452 --> 00:04:33.846
I think that nobody ever wants
to take that away from men.

00:04:33.846 --> 00:04:36.435
I think that what we want
to do in the world now

00:04:36.435 --> 00:04:38.761
is start to understand
what is masculinity.

00:04:38.761 --> 00:04:40.577
And it's always been
really associated with

00:04:40.577 --> 00:04:42.863
this very machismo space.

00:04:42.863 --> 00:04:45.039
And now there's different
kinds of men in the world.

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:46.888
There's not just biological men.

00:04:46.888 --> 00:04:48.172
There's also trans men

00:04:48.172 --> 00:04:50.303
or people who wanna be masculine.

00:04:50.303 --> 00:04:52.223
So I think what's happening now

00:04:52.223 --> 00:04:54.234
is people are pushing against change.

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:57.070
'Cause change is scary, and
people don't understand.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.112
And so I think men, biological men,

00:04:59.112 --> 00:05:02.472
feel under attack, when I that's
not what's happening here.

00:05:02.472 --> 00:05:05.181
- The point that you made is 100% correct.

00:05:05.181 --> 00:05:06.501
There are different phases

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.405
and people are experiencing
in different ways.

00:05:08.405 --> 00:05:11.047
The feminist movement is, I think,

00:05:11.047 --> 00:05:13.468
they are attacking masculinity within men.

00:05:13.468 --> 00:05:15.666
I don't want a man to open a door for me.

00:05:15.666 --> 00:05:17.061
I don't need a man in my life.

00:05:17.061 --> 00:05:18.614
I can do all these different things.

00:05:18.614 --> 00:05:20.211
What they're doing is attacking men

00:05:20.211 --> 00:05:21.402
and that's what's causing a problem.

00:05:21.402 --> 00:05:23.859
- What part of the feminist
group feels like it's attacking?

00:05:23.859 --> 00:05:25.430
'Cause I know that most feminism

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.397
is like wanting equal pay or-

00:05:27.397 --> 00:05:29.732
- Well, you just said
that women not needing men

00:05:29.732 --> 00:05:30.912
is somehow empowering.

00:05:30.912 --> 00:05:33.883
Having a man is somehow less empowering

00:05:33.883 --> 00:05:35.670
or being an individual is somehow less.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.236
- But that's how women feel.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.640
Women actually are saying that
because that's how they feel.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:40.473
It's like-
- That's not

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:41.347
how every woman feels,

00:05:41.347 --> 00:05:42.180
that's just an assumption-
- But no one's

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.638
saying every woman.

00:05:43.638 --> 00:05:44.783
Women speak for themselves.

00:05:44.783 --> 00:05:46.923
So all of you are gonna
have different opinions

00:05:46.923 --> 00:05:48.482
as biological men.

00:05:48.482 --> 00:05:50.138
Women all have different opinions.

00:05:50.138 --> 00:05:53.932
You'll see a very specific
group of women saying this.

00:05:53.932 --> 00:05:55.492
- You did just say that's how women feel.

00:05:55.492 --> 00:05:56.806
So are you speaking on
behalf of all women?

00:05:56.806 --> 00:05:57.877
- No, I'm not.

00:05:57.877 --> 00:05:59.432
Let me take that back.

00:05:59.432 --> 00:06:01.805
The women who are saying
that feel that way.

00:06:01.805 --> 00:06:06.361
- Why do you feel that women
in general feel disempowered?

00:06:06.361 --> 00:06:07.843
- No, I don't think in general.

00:06:07.843 --> 00:06:10.084
No, no, no, that's a
generalized statement.

00:06:10.084 --> 00:06:10.917
You can't say that, I said women-

00:06:10.917 --> 00:06:11.980
- But you're the one-
- No, I did not.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.700
I said the women who say that.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.335
- You associated somehow,

00:06:15.335 --> 00:06:17.463
women are now embracing masculinity,

00:06:17.463 --> 00:06:19.725
which means that they
are now more empowered

00:06:19.725 --> 00:06:20.558
because they don't need a man or if-

00:06:20.558 --> 00:06:22.084
- They don't need a man.

00:06:22.084 --> 00:06:23.596
Men feel empowered when women need them.

00:06:23.596 --> 00:06:25.270
- But I don't think
that women's empowerment

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:27.108
comes from having a man
or not having a man.

00:06:27.108 --> 00:06:29.589
So why is it always associated that

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:32.021
a woman's now empowered
because she doesn't need a man.

00:06:32.021 --> 00:06:33.640
A woman has always been empowered.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.255
Women have never been-
But they've never felt that-

00:06:35.255 --> 00:06:36.838
- That's not true,

00:06:36.838 --> 00:06:37.820
that's not true.
- I mean if we go back

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.427
to the 1920s, if you're gonna do that,

00:06:39.427 --> 00:06:40.260
but that's not-
- But of course-

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.262
- We're talking about society right now.

00:06:42.262 --> 00:06:43.447
- Right now, you actually think

00:06:43.447 --> 00:06:44.336
women are empowered right now?

00:06:44.336 --> 00:06:46.214
- Absolutely, women are empowered.

00:06:46.214 --> 00:06:47.047
- 'Cause of the vice president?

00:06:47.047 --> 00:06:48.808
And how long did it take for
her to become a vice president?

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:51.003
(whoosh air)

00:06:51.003 --> 00:06:52.322
- [Announcer] "There is a right

00:06:52.322 --> 00:06:54.572
and wrong way to be a man."

00:06:57.111 --> 00:06:59.778
Take a second to think about it.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.054
- I think that when I originally

00:07:07.054 --> 00:07:10.916
heard the question being
asked, I didn't agree with it,

00:07:10.916 --> 00:07:13.916
but men are not abusive individuals.

00:07:14.787 --> 00:07:17.465
Men are not to be cowards.

00:07:17.465 --> 00:07:19.766
Men are to lead their families.

00:07:19.766 --> 00:07:22.402
And men who do not display that,

00:07:22.402 --> 00:07:24.787
I don't believe that they
are men, in my opinion.

00:07:24.787 --> 00:07:26.986
And all of the qualities
that I see in my father

00:07:26.986 --> 00:07:28.675
is what I believe a man should be.

00:07:28.675 --> 00:07:30.466
- All of those characteristics
are what make a man.

00:07:30.466 --> 00:07:33.642
And when I see a man be
a coward in the truth,

00:07:33.642 --> 00:07:37.388
and just speaking the truth or
sticking up for what's right,

00:07:37.388 --> 00:07:39.578
especially today in America,
with everything going on,

00:07:39.578 --> 00:07:40.991
I'm like, those are not men.

00:07:40.991 --> 00:07:41.824
(whoosh air)

00:07:41.824 --> 00:07:42.657
My name is Clarkson.

00:07:42.657 --> 00:07:45.213
I'm 24 years old and
I'm a conservative man.

00:07:45.213 --> 00:07:47.651
My biggest question for the other side

00:07:47.651 --> 00:07:48.991
really is are you happy?

00:07:48.991 --> 00:07:51.974
Anybody that wants to
fundamentally change society

00:07:51.974 --> 00:07:54.842
and change gender roles,
to me that's not happiness.

00:07:54.842 --> 00:07:56.896
And if we wanna fight for acceptance,

00:07:56.896 --> 00:07:58.971
we need to start with acceptance,

00:07:58.971 --> 00:08:02.471
which is accepting society for what it is.

00:08:05.199 --> 00:08:06.587
- At the end of the day, we're all men.

00:08:06.587 --> 00:08:10.284
And I don't believe there's
any wrong way to be a man.

00:08:10.284 --> 00:08:13.450
We're just redefining
what it means to be a man.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.759
- But there are things
that naturally come to men.

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:19.106
So when you say we're just
redefining what being a man is,

00:08:19.106 --> 00:08:20.627
you have to understand you're redefining

00:08:20.627 --> 00:08:23.662
a fabric and society that
has kept the human race

00:08:23.662 --> 00:08:25.300
and got it to where it is today.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.413
So just like aimlessly throwing out,

00:08:27.413 --> 00:08:29.310
"Oh, well we're just redefining
what it is to be a man."

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.036
That's not just like a light subject

00:08:31.036 --> 00:08:32.346
that we should be talking about.

00:08:32.346 --> 00:08:33.639
- But why do you think
we have to stay the same?

00:08:33.639 --> 00:08:35.104
Why do we need to have the same thing

00:08:35.104 --> 00:08:36.154
for 100s and 100s of years?

00:08:36.154 --> 00:08:37.464
- Do you not see the state-
- It's not same thing.

00:08:37.464 --> 00:08:38.778
- It's just the same.
- It's just keeping

00:08:38.778 --> 00:08:40.061
the same qualities.

00:08:40.061 --> 00:08:42.562
- But do you see the
state of our world today?

00:08:42.562 --> 00:08:43.761
It's not perfect.

00:08:43.761 --> 00:08:46.968
It has been led by men
throughout all of history

00:08:46.968 --> 00:08:49.029
and look where it's gone.

00:08:49.029 --> 00:08:51.684
- So we're talking about redesigning

00:08:51.684 --> 00:08:52.628
what it means to be a man.

00:08:52.628 --> 00:08:55.279
So what do you wanna
bring to traditional men?

00:08:55.279 --> 00:08:57.769
- I think it's embracing
that you can be vulnerable.

00:08:57.769 --> 00:08:59.804
I think that a lot of men
wanna portray strength,

00:08:59.804 --> 00:09:01.117
strength, strength.

00:09:01.117 --> 00:09:02.399
But men are people.

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:03.711
And I know that men have feelings.

00:09:03.711 --> 00:09:05.636
- Being a man and masculinity,

00:09:05.636 --> 00:09:06.827
those are two different things.

00:09:06.827 --> 00:09:10.698
And I believe that we can
redefine whatever that means

00:09:10.698 --> 00:09:13.881
to anybody by including other types of men

00:09:13.881 --> 00:09:15.317
or other types of masculinity.

00:09:15.317 --> 00:09:16.481
I, myself am a father.

00:09:16.481 --> 00:09:17.357
I have a child.

00:09:17.357 --> 00:09:19.309
Some people would disagree
with me being a father

00:09:19.309 --> 00:09:20.925
because I am transgender.

00:09:20.925 --> 00:09:23.641
But that being said, I present
to the world as a male.

00:09:23.641 --> 00:09:25.072
My child sees me as a man.

00:09:25.072 --> 00:09:27.090
- There's proper ways
to be vulnerable, right?

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:28.167
You don't have to break down

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:29.366
in front of your family and cry.

00:09:29.366 --> 00:09:31.163
It's okay to suffer in silence as well.

00:09:31.163 --> 00:09:33.753
Strong men, I believe exude the qualities

00:09:33.753 --> 00:09:35.398
that you guys are referring to.

00:09:35.398 --> 00:09:38.720
I think the problem is
overcorrection, right?

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.473
Some people believe that men need to cry

00:09:41.473 --> 00:09:43.806
and lay on the ground and
be feminine, like women.

00:09:43.806 --> 00:09:44.639
(whoosh air)

00:09:44.639 --> 00:09:45.576
My name is Brandon.

00:09:45.576 --> 00:09:48.518
I'm 34 years old and
I'm a conservative man.

00:09:48.518 --> 00:09:50.943
I had a lot of curiosities about

00:09:50.943 --> 00:09:53.018
what it's like to be a person

00:09:53.018 --> 00:09:54.871
who believes that they're trans man.

00:09:54.871 --> 00:09:57.678
I feel like God has created
all of us very uniquely.

00:09:57.678 --> 00:09:59.793
And although I have beliefs

00:09:59.793 --> 00:10:01.761
and I follow the Bible to the tee,

00:10:01.761 --> 00:10:04.311
I still wanna know from other people

00:10:04.311 --> 00:10:07.225
what their experiences are,
doesn't mean I have to agree,

00:10:07.225 --> 00:10:10.393
but I really want to know
what other people are feeling

00:10:10.393 --> 00:10:12.763
from the person who's
experiencing it real time.

00:10:12.763 --> 00:10:13.785
(whoosh air)

00:10:13.785 --> 00:10:16.952
- [Announcer] "I have male privilege."

00:10:21.677 --> 00:10:22.510
- Oh, sit over here.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.702
(both laughs)

00:10:24.702 --> 00:10:25.593
I've lived both lives.

